Hikari is an independent implementation of a game launcher for the Ryoku
Linux desktop. It re-implements orchestration behaviour documented by the
following projects, whose source was used as a behavioural reference only
(no source code is copied from them):

- Heroic Games Launcher (GPL-3.0) — engine invocation (legendary, gogdl,
  nile, comet), on-disk config formats, launch pipeline, install progress
  parsing. https://github.com/Heroic-Games-Launcher/HeroicGamesLauncher
- OptiTux (no license file; behaviour reference only) — OptiScaler
  integration behaviour: GPU detection, per-game install layout, INI
  profile patching. https://github.com/Spexxl/OptiTux
- Ryoku (GPL-3.0) — daemon socket conventions, TOML config persistence
  pattern, packaging conventions. https://github.com/Ryoku-dev/ryoku

Hikari runs, but does not distribute, the following third-party tools:
legendary, gogdl, nile, comet, umu-launcher, Proton, Wine. Their licenses
apply to themselves.
